    "draft": true,
    "body": "## Purpose\nQualify the reviewed capacity guards through the unchanged original Host Process workflow after the accepted test-only RED on PR #1206.\n\n## Frozen scope\nOnly the two approved capacity guards and their unchanged regression tests differ in executable source from the fixed 22078 CI base. Original provider fixtures, 15-second budgets, custody/currentness and workflows remain unchanged.\n\n## Evidence and limits\nPR #1206 original Windows ARM and Darwin x64 each reached the full eight-file Main run: 79 PASS, two specific FAIL, zero SKIP at 7/8-slot handshake admission. This new Draft PR obtains resulting-source GREEN; it does not replace #1192 or qualify later native, UI or release gates. Eight existing workflow triggers are disclosed in the published R1. Real Claude/Codex remain forbidden; permitted OpenCode uses finite localhost fixtures.\n\n## Lifecycle\nKeep this head/base and root-authored Draft PR metadata fixed while the useful cohort runs. No rerun, dispatch, Ready, merge, review requests, auto-merge, default/base change or compiler retry is authorized by opening this venue.",
